 ## Overview
-Composition via Convolution (Power Form) is a method for evaluating the composition of a trivariate polynomial field with a linear ray parameterization, transforming a 3D function into a univariate function along a ray [S1]. It solves the problem of efficient numerical evaluation in direct volume ray casting by using convolution operators to reduce computation and register usage compared to naive substitution [S1]. Unlike [Feed-Backward Reconstruction](2433-feed-backward-reconstruction.md), which focuses on reconstruction filters, this method specifically optimizes the algebraic evaluation of the polynomial composition itself [S1].
