 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The method significantly reduces the number of multiplications and additions compared to naive substitution. For a degree $d=3$ polynomial, it requires 234 multiplications and 360 additions, compared to 1839 multiplications and 990 additions for the naive method [S1].
